runtimeInvoke.description:
Calling a `dedicated` agent's runtime: maxAttempts (total, default 1 — InvokeAgentRuntime is not idempotent, so a retry bills a second model call and returns whichever answered last) and readTimeoutSeconds (default 600: a dedicated agent that makes several tool calls and writes a long answer takes minutes, and 120 timed out such an agent mid-answer).

Read by: config.py RUNTIME_INVOKE -> agentcore_agent

Default: {"maxAttempts": 1, "readTimeoutSeconds": 600}

a2aInvoke.description:
Calling a `runtime: "a2a"` agent: timeoutSeconds per request (default 30 — keep it ABOVE the remote agent's own timeout so the side that gives up first can say why), pollIntervalSeconds (2) and maxPollSeconds (300) for a task that is still working.

Read by: config.py A2A_INVOKE -> a2a_agent

Default: {"timeoutSeconds": 30, "pollIntervalSeconds": 2, "maxPollSeconds": 300}

insights.description:
AgentCore Insights timings: lookbackHours (168), pollTimeoutSeconds (900), pollIntervalSeconds (20).

Read by: config.py INSIGHTS -> features/optimization/insights.py

Default: {"lookbackHours": 168, "pollTimeoutSeconds": 900, "pollIntervalSeconds": 20}

policy.description:
The Cedar policy engine on the Gateway: enabled; mode ENFORCE (a DENY blocks the call) or LOG_ONLY (evaluate and log — the safe way to roll out); and `custom`, your own policies next to the permit generated for each tool: [{"name": "noBigRefunds", "description": "...", "statement": "forbid(principal, action == AgentCore::Action::\"refunds___issueRefund\", resource == AgentCore::Gateway::\"{{gateway}}\") when { context.input.amount > 500 };"}]. Actions are "<toolKey>___<toolName>" (one tool) or "<toolKey>" with `in` (all of its tools); the resource is always AgentCore::Gateway::"{{gateway}}", filled in at deploy. A forbid always wins over a permit; anything no policy permits is denied. To replace a tool's generated permit with your own, set that tool's policy.permit to false.

Read by: policy.tf / tool-plane.ts (custom -> one AgentCore policy each, custom_<name>_<hash>); mode reaches the app as GATEWAY_POLICY_MODE

Default: {"enabled": true, "mode": "ENFORCE"}
